            title: `Q8. Discuss Meetings: Kinds, Quorum, and Proxy. (Part B: 10m / Part C: 10m)`,
            content: `Types of meetings: (1) Board meetings - meetings of directors. (2) General meetings - meetings of shareholders. General meetings include: (a) Annual General Meeting (AGM - Section 96) - must be held every year, within 6 months of the close of the financial year. Not more than 15 months gap between two AGMs. Business transacted: adoption of accounts, declaration of dividend, appointment of auditors, appointment of directors. (b) Extraordinary General Meeting (EGM - Section 100) - for urgent business that cannot wait until the next AGM. Can be called by the Board, or on requisition of members holding at least 10% of paid-up share capital.

Quorum (Section 103): The minimum number of members required to constitute a valid meeting. For public companies: 5 members personally present (up to 1000 members), 15 (1001-5000), 30 (above 5000). For private companies: 2 members personally present. If quorum is not present within half an hour of the appointed time, the meeting stands adjourned to the same day next week, same time, same place. At the adjourned meeting, the members present shall be the quorum.

Proxy (Section 105): A member entitled to attend and vote at a meeting may appoint another person as his proxy to attend and vote on his behalf. A proxy need not be a member of the company. The instrument of proxy must be deposited at the registered office not less than 48 hours before the meeting. A member can appoint only one proxy (but can hold proxies of multiple members). Key rule: When the member personally attends the meeting, the proxy stands automatically revoked.

EXAM TIP: PART C PROBLEM: 'A appoints B as proxy. Just before the meeting, A comes to attend personally. What is the position of the proxy?' ANSWER: When the principal (member) attends the meeting personally, the authority of the proxy stands automatically revoked. A proxy is merely an agent, and the principal's personal presence supersedes the agent's authority. B's proxy is revoked, and only A can vote.`,
